From 0905159dd3309993c4adcc4ecd0898726904f7ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 20:40:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(chat): drop profile and agent name rows from sessions
 and bubbles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The session-list subtitle showed the profile name (e.g. "default") and every
message bubble printed an author line above it — the profile/alias for user
messages and the runtime name (Hermes/Ekko/Claude/...) for assistant messages.
Both are noise in a single-user, single-agent chat view, so remove them:

- SessionListItem: drop the profile row and the showProfile prop; the
  subtitle row now only renders when a category label exists.
- MessageItem: drop the author rows, the assistantAgent/userProfileName props
  and the .message-author* styles.
- MessageList/HistoryMessageList: drop the now-orphan profile computed,
  profilesStore usage and prop passing.
- tests: remove the suites that only asserted the author rows; keep the
  chat-agent-label unit suite (labels still drive the run indicator).
- harness: re-home the one ui-theme baseline key that included the deleted
  .session-item-profile-name selector.
